I suppose there's no doubt here that Nethack is built on large amounts
of fantasy, magic, and non-realism; and some explanations can only be
answered as "It's Magic!".

A consistent[*] system is helpful to infer solutions from situations.
That's a good basis to _play intuitively_, not only for unspoiled
players like "Ellora". Realism is our _default system_ that provides
consistency. IMO, it's basically a Good Thing. Making intuitive play
possible on a consistently designed game adds to gameplay; sometimes
we even don't notice that fact any more, because we accept it as a
matter of course.

[*] I.e. consistent w.r.t. cause and expected effect.

But realism in any case, of course, need/should not be the design
principle for any feature in the game. I just cannot agree to the
"minus points" you assigned in that case.

